    <Vertical id="reasons_list">
    <Markdown>
## Select Focus Areas
### List of causes of high school dropout
 - Some school systems can't accommodate students with physical or other disabilities
 - Students need to earn money right away to help their family
 - Schools use curricula that students don't see as relevant
 - Student's environment with gang activity, neighborhood instability
 - Conditions like depression, anxiety, or ADHD interfere with engagement
 - Students lack family, friends, or teacher support
 - Negative peer influences encourage dropping out
 - Cultural responsibilities more important than high school
 - Legal trouble makes it difficult to continue school
 - Lack of school funding for support services
 - Teen pregnancy with no school support
 - Substance abuse issues
      </Markdown>
    </Vertical>

